  "properties": {
    "title": "pgRouting project status",
    "description": "pgRouting project status presentation.  \r\n\r\nCome and find out the latest news on the project as well as future plans, and how to get involved!\n\npgRouting, the PostgreSQL/PostGIS driven extension for graphs and routing.\r\nAt the end of 2025, we moved to pgRouting 4.0 with new additional functions and a standardized structure on the function signatures.\r\nAdditionally there are more sub-products from pgRouting that are available for public use.\r\n\r\nThis presentation will provide an update on:\r\n- The current status\r\n  - pgRouting\r\n  - osm2pgrouting\r\n  - pgroutingLayers\r\n  - vrpRouting\r\n- Our classification: official, proposed, experimental\r\n- Changes and migration from 3.8 to 4.0 versions\r\n- GSoC-OSGeo program: for students to get involved",
